msgid "settings.access_control.blacklist.community.description"
msgstr "Curated lists maintained outside BunkerWeb and refreshed for you. They feed the same matching as the entries below."

msgid "settings.access_control.blacklist.community.title"
msgstr "Community lists"

msgid "settings.access_control.blacklist.enforcement.description"
msgstr "The blacklist runs after the whitelist, so a client that is whitelisted is never blocked here. On each row, the exception lists override that row's own entries and downloaded lists."

msgid "settings.access_control.country.conflict.clear"
msgstr "Clear the block list"

msgid "settings.access_control.country.conflict.description"
msgstr "Both country lists are stored, and only the allow list is enforced: the block list below is never consulted while an allow list is set."

msgid "settings.access_control.country.description"
msgstr "One rule, not two lists. Allowing a set of countries denies every other country and makes a stored block list dead configuration — BunkerWeb checks the allow list first and never reaches the block list."

msgid "settings.access_control.country.exceptions.description"
msgstr "Requests whose URI matches one of these patterns skip the country rule entirely."

msgid "settings.access_control.country.exceptions.title"
msgstr "Exceptions"

msgid "settings.access_control.country.mode.all"
msgstr "No country rule"

msgid "settings.access_control.country.mode.block"
msgstr "Block these countries"

msgid "settings.access_control.country.mode.only"
msgstr "Allow only these countries"

msgid "settings.access_control.country.picker_label"
msgstr "Country rule"

msgid "settings.access_control.country.title"
msgstr "Country rule"

msgid "settings.access_control.enforcement.title"
msgstr "Enforcement"

msgid "settings.access_control.greylist.enforcement.description"
msgstr "The greylist is deny-by-default: while it is on, anything that matches none of the entries below is denied, on HTTP and on stream traffic alike. Add the entries first, then turn it on — a save that enables it with every list empty is refused."

msgid "settings.access_control.greylist.locked_out"
msgstr "Greylisting is on and no entry is configured, so every request to this service is denied. Add at least one entry below, or turn greylisting off."

msgid "settings.access_control.kind.asn"
msgstr "Autonomous systems (ASN)"

msgid "settings.access_control.kind.ip"
msgstr "IP addresses and networks"

msgid "settings.access_control.kind.rdns"
msgstr "Reverse DNS"

msgid "settings.access_control.kind.uri"
msgstr "URIs"

msgid "settings.access_control.kind.user_agent"
msgstr "User agents"

msgid "settings.access_control.kinds.description"
msgstr "One section per kind of match. In each, the entries you type and the lists BunkerWeb downloads are checked together; a client matching either one matches the section."

msgid "settings.access_control.kinds.title"
msgstr "What is matched"

msgid "settings.access_control.order.current"
msgstr "current page"

msgid "settings.access_control.order.description"
msgstr "By default every request walks these four checks in this order, and the first one to decide, decides. A whitelist match ends the walk immediately: the request is allowed and the three checks after it never run. The order itself is configurable per service, through PLUGINS_ORDER_ACCESS and PLUGINS_ORDER_PREREAD."

msgid "settings.access_control.order.off"
msgstr "Off"

msgid "settings.access_control.order.on"
msgstr "On"

msgid "settings.access_control.order.title"
msgstr "Decision order"

msgid "settings.access_control.stage.blacklist"
msgstr "Blacklist"

msgid "settings.access_control.stage.country"
msgstr "Country"

msgid "settings.access_control.stage.greylist"
msgstr "Greylist"

msgid "settings.access_control.stage.whitelist"
msgstr "Whitelist"

msgid "settings.access_control.unplaced.description"
msgstr "Declared by the plugin but not yet given a place on this page. They still save normally."

msgid "settings.access_control.unplaced.title"
msgstr "Other settings"

msgid "settings.access_control.whitelist.enforcement.description"
msgstr "The whitelist runs first and overrides everything else: a match is allowed straight through, so blacklist, greylist and country never see the request. Bans are the one exception, and only by IP — a client matched here by reverse DNS, ASN, user agent or URI is still blocked while it is banned. Keep this list to the clients that must never be locked out."

